+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9392759521f7445","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# T9: SSG Toolkit\n     2→\n     3→Add 8 plugins to an existing Static Site Generator toolkit.\n     4→\n     5→## Starting State\n     6→- `src/core/` contains the build engine, types, and templates (~600 lines)\n     7→- 15 existing tests in `tests/core.test.ts` — these must continue to pass\n     8→- Plugin test files in `tests/plugins/` define the expected behavior\n     9→\n    10→## Requirements\n    11→\n    12→Build 8 plugins in `src/plugins/`, each implementing the `Plugin` interface from `src/core/types.ts`.\n    13→\n    14→### Wave 1 (no dependencies)\n    15→1. **markdown-ext** — Markdown → HTML with footnotes and admonition containers\n    16→2. **asset-pipeline** — Rewrite asset URLs and generate manifest\n    17→3. **syntax-highlight** — Add language classes to code blocks\n    18→4. **taxonomy** — Build tag/category indices and generate tag pages\n    19→\n    20→### Wave 2 (depend on Wave 1)\n    21→5. **rss-feed** — Generate RSS 2.0 feed (depends: markdown-ext, taxonomy)\n    22→6. **search-index** — Generate search index JSON (depends: markdown-ext, syntax-highlight)\n    23→\n    24→### Wave 3 (depend on Wave 2)\n    25→7. **sitemap** — Generate sitemap XML (depends: taxonomy, rss-feed)\n    26→8. **dev-server** — Generate dev server config (depends: asset-pipeline, search-index)\n    27→\n    28→### Plugin Interface\n    29→Each plugin must export a `createXxxPlugin()` factory function that returns a `Plugin` object.\n    30→\n    31→## Validation\n    32→- `npm test` — all tests must pass (15 existing + 60 new)\n    33→- `npm run build` — must compile\n    34→- `npm run lint` — must be clean\n    35→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d970cfb0b8866d7","session_id":"4749bb77-0a2a-4de5-8761-981132f57a64","uuid":"1c20bce5-14a4-4d1b-aaad-bc01b1ce3982"}
