+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2d88ea1d094af78","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→export interface SiteConfig {\n     2→  title: string;\n     3→  baseUrl: string;\n     4→  outputDir: string;\n     5→  contentDir: string;\n     6→  templateDir: string;\n     7→}\n     8→\n     9→export interface ContentFile {\n    10→  slug: string;\n    11→  title: string;\n    12→  content: string;        // raw content (markdown or html)\n    13→  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;\n    14→  date?: string;\n    15→  tags?: string[];\n    16→  template?: string;\n    17→}\n    18→\n    19→export interface BuildContext {\n    20→  config: SiteConfig;\n    21→  files: ContentFile[];\n    22→  output: Map<string, string>;  // output path -> rendered content\n    23→  assets: Map<string, Buffer>;  // output path -> binary data\n    24→  data: Map<string, unknown>;   // shared plugin data store\n    25→}\n    26→\n    27→export interface PluginHooks {\n    28→  beforeBuild?: (ctx: BuildContext) => Promise<void> | void;\n    29→  transformContent?: (file: ContentFile, ctx: BuildContext) => Promise<ContentFile> | ContentFile;\n    30→  afterBuild?: (ctx: BuildContext) => Promise<void> | void;\n    31→}\n    32→\n    33→export interface Plugin {\n    34→  name: string;\n    35→  version: string;\n    36→  dependencies: string[];  // names of plugins this depends on\n    37→  hooks: PluginHooks;\n    38→}\n    39→\n    40→export interface Template {\n    41→  name: string;\n    42→  render: (content: string, data: Record<string, unknown>) => string;\n    43→}\n    44→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"